    "narrative": "It is a challenging mid-July slate for the Austin Waves as we navigate a day where our primary offensive engines, **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson**, are all inactive due to team off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined on the IL, our offensive ceiling is heavily suppressed. Given the constraints, **Andy Pages** (43.41) and **Drake Baldwin** (40.51) represent our strongest available plays, though both face a significant hurdle in Cease. While **Andy Pages** benefits from a slight park factor boost and consistent recency performance, the elite stuff of the opposing arm keeps his upside capped. **Drake Baldwin** remains a marginal play at best; his position in the nine-hole combined with the high-caliber SP_xERA of 2.96 makes him a start purely for volume necessity rather than projected efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's lineup involved managing our depth against the aggressive scoring floor. Both **Jackson Merrill** and **Jordan Westburg** were considered for the final utility spots, but current projections suggest that preserving our remaining game caps is the more analytical play until we see the full lineup confirmation for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Jacob Wilson**. The primary risk today is the stifling impact of the opposing starter; with an xERA under 3.00, we are banking on efficiency through plate discipline rather than power hitting. Should the official lineups reveal a promotion for **Jorge Polanco** or **Josh Lowe** into the heart of their respective orders, we will re-evaluate, but for now, the Waves will exercise caution to ensure our roster depth\u2014including **Nasim Nunez**, **Cole Carrigg**, **Heliot Ramos**, and **Josh Jung**\u2014is available for matchups with more favorable pitching profiles later in the week. We continue to monitor the status of **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Brayan Rocchio** to see if late-breaking lineup data warrants a pivot from our current bench configuration involving **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Lara**, and **Denzer Guzman**.",
